WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.500
Large context can fail in ways that are easy to miss.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:06.440
One commonly discussed issue is the lost-in-the-middle effect,

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:10.760
where important information buried deep inside a long context may be underused or missed.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:14.870
The exact behavior depends on the model and task, but the practical lesson is clear:

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:16.430
placement and emphasis still matter.

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:19.101
Do not assume that every token receives equal attention.

00:00:19.101 --> 00:00:23.795
Irrelevant context can reduce reliability by distracting the model or encouraging shallow

00:00:23.795 --> 00:00:24.600
synthesis.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.519
Stale context can conflict with current facts, decisions, or requirements.

00:00:28.519 --> 00:00:31.120
Conflicting instructions can cause the model to follow the wrong priority.

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:35.840
If a prompt contains old meeting notes, current policy, examples, and user preferences,

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:39.100
the model needs help understanding which material controls the answer.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:42.540
Prompt injection and context poisoning are serious concerns when retrieved or

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:44.530
user-supplied material is included.

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:49.080
A document may contain text that tries to redirect the model, reveal hidden instructions,

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:52.000
ignore the user's task, or change output requirements.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.756
Large context increases the amount of untrusted text that may be present.

00:00:55.756 --> 00:00:59.520
Workflows should separate instructions from data and treat retrieved text as evidence,

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:00.520
not authority.

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:04.575
Hallucinated synthesis can happen when the model blends sources into an answer that sounds

00:01:04.575 --> 00:01:06.275
coherent but is not fully supported.

00:01:06.275 --> 00:01:09.580
Overconfident summaries may hide uncertainty or omit exceptions.

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:13.635
Missed details can be especially costly when the user assumes a large context window means

00:01:13.635 --> 00:01:14.925
the model checked everything.

00:01:14.925 --> 00:01:19.435
More context can improve performance, but it can also reduce reliability if selection,

00:01:19.435 --> 00:01:20.470
structure, and review are weak.
